  "facts": [
    "The Gleinalm Tunnel, stretching 8,320 meters, opened in 1978, cutting the Graz–Murau journey by roughly twenty minutes and reshaping regional travel.",
    "Only one tube carries oncoming traffic at 80 km/h, and drivers pay a €10 toll, a unique combination of safety and cost in Austrian highway design.",
    "Construction of a second tube began on 21 September 2013, and by 21 July 2017 both tubes operated together, with the original slated for renovation thereafter."
